# SC2016 ("expressions don't expand in single quotes") is a false positive
# throughout tests/: several tests deliberately build a zsh command string in
# single quotes and hand it to a *different* shell (a `zsh -c` sub-invocation,
# or a fake compinit interception) to expand there, not in this file's own
# bash context. Expanding it here would be the actual bug. Disabled
# repo-wide rather than per-line: the pattern recurs across test_loader.sh
# and test_modules.sh, and CI's `shellcheck install.sh claude/statusline.sh
# tests/*.sh` (.github/workflows/ci.yml) must stay green for a reason, not
# because every one of these was individually silenced.
disable=SC2016
